<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Udai Singh II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1522">1522</a>–<a href="/years/1572">1572</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Udai Singh II of Mewar · Of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sisodia-dynasty">Sisodia dynasty</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Udai Singh II was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharana">Maharana</a> of Mewar until his death in 1572 and the founder of the city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/udaipur">Udaipur</a> in 1559. A son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rana-sanga">Rana Sanga</a>, he escaped as a child from the usurper Banvir, who had killed his brother Vikramaditya, and later won back the throne. When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akbar">Akbar</a> besieged and took Chittor in 1567–1568, he withdrew to the hills, and Udaipur became Mewar's new capital. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharana-pratap">Maharana Pratap</a> continued the resistance to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughals</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/udai-singh-ii.jpg" alt="Udai Singh II" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tanvi12 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rana-udai-singh-ii.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Successive rulers built some of the largest reservoirs of pre-modern India: Lake Pichola was enlarged when <b>Udai Singh II</b> founded Udaipur, Raj Singh I created Rajsamand Lake in the 1660s and 1670s, and Jai Singh built Jaisamand Lake in the late seventeenth century.</blockquote><a href="/empire/udaipur-state">Udaipur State · Socioeconomy</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Chittorgarh, in what is now <a href="/countries/india">India</a>. Died in Gogunda, in what is now <a href="/countries/india">India</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=24.89,74.62&amp;year=1554" aria-label="Chittorgarh on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6530 1248 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Udai Singh II"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6980 1518h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6980 1518h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=24.89,74.62&amp;year=1554">What was here in 1554? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
